# Copy to .env (git-ignored) for `docker compose`. Server secrets (device tokens, intervals.icu, Strava,
# Google, Telegram, LLM endpoint) live here and nowhere else; the repository is public.

# Goes into the database URL as it is, so use URL-safe characters: openssl rand -hex 24
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me

# The devices that may call /v1: name:token, comma-separated, each token at least 32 characters.
# Make one with `openssl rand -base64 36`, then type it into the tablet's Settings, Sync (never
# into a chat or a commit). Empty means every /v1 request is answered 401.
# DEVICE_TOKENS=tablet:<the output of openssl rand -base64 36>

# intervals.icu (ADR 0016): rides are sent there and the plan is read from its calendar. Off while the key
# is empty or missing (rides are still queued and go out once it is set). The key is in intervals.icu,
# Settings, Developer Settings, API Key; never paste it into a chat, an issue or a commit.
# INTERVALS_API_KEY=<your personal API key>
# Your athlete id (i12345, in the address of your intervals.icu pages); 0 means the athlete the key belongs to.
# INTERVALS_ATHLETE_ID=0
# Only to go through a proxy; the default is https://intervals.icu
# INTERVALS_BASE_URL=https://intervals.icu
# How often the plan (today and the next 14 days) is read, in minutes (1 to 1440). Default 15.
# PLAN_REFRESH_MINUTES=15
# Your time zone (IANA name): which day is "today" for the plan and which day a ride, a night of sleep or a watch workout belongs to. Default UTC.
# TIMEZONE=Europe/Paris

# Wellness and recovery (ADR 0023, docs/deploy.md section 16). The phone uploads its Health Connect records with the device token; nothing
# here is a secret and none of it is needed for that. Which source a daily figure is taken from: the first in the list that has one; after
# a semicolon one metric gets an order of its own (restingHr=intervals,healthconnect). Default: healthconnect,intervals
# WELLNESS_SOURCE_ORDER=healthconnect,intervals
# How often intervals.icu's wellness is read, in hours (1 to 168; only with an intervals.icu key). Default 6.
# WELLNESS_PULL_HOURS=6
# The window of a personal baseline in days (28 to 60) and the nights before any recovery verdict (7 to 28). Defaults 42 and 14.
# WELLNESS_BASELINE_DAYS=42
# WELLNESS_NIGHTS_NEEDED=14

# Written insights, alerts and discussion topics (ADR 0025, docs/deploy.md section 17). They work with NO setting: without an LLM the notes
# are written from fixed templates and no health data leaves the server. To have a language model write them, set the first and the
# third of these (any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions server). THE FACTS OF YOUR TRAINING AND RECOVERY ARE SENT TO THAT ADDRESS and to
# no other. https only (http for localhost). The key is a secret: fill it in an editor on the host, never in a chat, an issue or a commit.
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=<the key of that endpoint, if it needs one>
# LLM_MODEL=<the model's name at that endpoint>
# Seconds one request may take (5 to 600). Default 60.
# LLM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=60
# The language of the notes: a name or a code (en, French, pt-BR). The fallback template is always English. Default en.
# INSIGHTS_LANGUAGE=en
# When the morning note is written, in TIMEZONE (HH:MM or off). The morning alerts are checked then too. Default 07:00.
# INSIGHT_MORNING_TIME=07:00
# false: no note or alert is written or sent (the ones already written are still served). Default true.
# INSIGHTS_ENABLED=true
# Words a written note may never contain, added to the built-in list (comma-separated, case-insensitive).
# INSIGHT_DENY_WORDS=
# Alerts (spec 6.6): a metric outside its own usual range, on its adverse side, for this many mornings in a row (2 to 14); plan drift:
# this many planned sessions missed in the last 7 days (1 to 7), or the load of those days this far above (5 to 300) or below (5 to 95)
# the plan, in percent. Defaults 3, 2, 30, 40.
# ALERT_STREAK_DAYS=3
# ALERT_MISSED_SESSIONS=2
# ALERT_LOAD_ABOVE_PERCENT=30
# ALERT_LOAD_BELOW_PERCENT=40

# The MCP server and its OAuth server (ADR 0018): AI clients (Claude's apps and others) plan workouts and read rides at
# <PUBLIC_BASE_URL>/mcp. Off, with its routes absent, unless BOTH of these are set.
# Your service's public address (https; no path):
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://overdrive.llmto.day
# The hash of the passphrase you type to approve each client. The server never holds the passphrase itself. Make the hash with
#   pnpm --filter @overdrive/server run hash-passphrase
# (or on the host: docker compose run --rm --no-deps server node dist/hash-passphrase.js) and paste the line it prints.
# OWNER_PASSPHRASE_HASH=scrypt:32768:8:1:<salt>:<hash>
# Only for an MCP client that cannot do OAuth and can send a fixed header: name:token, each token at least 32 characters
# (openssl rand -base64 36). Opens /mcp and nothing else.
# MCP_STATIC_TOKENS=claude:<the output of openssl rand -base64 36>
# Google Calendar (ADR 0019, docs/deploy.md section 14): the plan is pushed one way to a dedicated calendar.
# On only when all four are set. Fill them in an editor on the host; never paste them into a chat, an issue or a commit.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=<OAuth client of type Desktop app, from the Google Cloud console>
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=<its secret>
# GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=<printed once by: pnpm --filter @overdrive/server run google-auth>
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID=<calendar settings, Integrate calendar: ...@group.calendar.google.com>
# The time a workout starts, in TIMEZONE: the event's start and the reference of the lead reminder. Default 07:00.
# GCAL_WORKOUT_START=07:00

# Telegram bot (ADR 0019, docs/deploy.md section 13). Off while the token is empty. With the token and no chat id the bot
# only listens and logs the chat id of whoever writes to it; copy yours here, then it answers that chat and nobody else.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=<from BotFather>
# TELEGRAM_OWNER_CHAT_ID=<your private chat id, a number>
# The evening-before reminder (HH:MM or off), and the second one this many minutes before the start (0 = off).
# REMINDER_EVENING_TIME=20:00
# REMINDER_LEAD_MINUTES=60
# The weekly summary: a day (mon ... sun) and a time (HH:MM or off).
# WEEKLY_SUMMARY_DAY=sun
# WEEKLY_SUMMARY_TIME=18:00

# The Strava upload (ADR 0020): each ride is posted to Strava as a virtual ride with a short description. Write-only: nothing is
# read from Strava. Off unless ALL THREE of these are set. Create the application at https://www.strava.com/settings/api (callback
# domain: localhost), then run once, in your own terminal, `pnpm --filter @overdrive/server run strava-auth` (or on the host:
# docker compose run --rm --no-deps -it server node dist/strava-auth.js); see docs/deploy.md section 15. Never paste these into a chat.
# STRAVA_CLIENT_ID=<the number shown as Client ID>
# STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET=<the Client Secret>
# Printed by strava-auth. Only seeds the first run: Strava rotates it and the server keeps the newest one itself.
# STRAVA_REFRESH_TOKEN=<the line strava-auth printed>
# true: also post the rides stored before Strava was turned on, at the next start. Default false (the history is not posted).
# STRAVA_BACKFILL=false

# Ports on the host's loopback (Caddy proxies to SERVER_PORT); change them when another project owns these.
SERVER_PORT=8080
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Live coach voice (spec section 12.1, planned for v0.4.0, stage A3: NOT read by the service yet). The owner's own TTS server,
# OpenAI-compatible (`POST /audio/speech`). Fill the key in an editor on the host; never paste it into a chat or a commit.
# TTS_BASE_URL=https://ai03.incoplax.com/v1
# TTS_API_KEY=<the key of that server>
# TTS_MODEL=VoxCPM2
# TTS_VOICE=<a voice name of that server>
